    exam_type: 'JAMB • WAEC • NECO Standard',
    class_level: 'SS1-SS3 Comprehensive',
    topic: 'DRAMA',
    subtopic: 'European Drama',
    summary_60s: 'The development of European drama can be traced to ritual performances associated with the Dionysian festivals in ancient Athens . Greek drama reached artistic maturity through tragedy , while Roman drama showed particular strength in comedy , as reflected in the surviving works ',
