    summary_60s: 'Narrative techniques or devices are tools that authors use to enhance their stories, creating vivid and engaging narratives. These techniques are the backbone of storytelling, guiding us through the intricate dance of plot, character, and theme. 1. Point of View (POV) The perspec',
